Repeat submission of
students’ NEA work

If students have not performed at their best during the assessment of NEA units, they
can improve their work and submit it to you again for assessment. They must have
your agreement and you must be sure it is in the student’s best interests.

We use the term ‘resubmission’ when referring to student work that has previously
been submitted to OCR for moderation. Following OCR moderation a student can
attempt to improve their work, for you to assess and provide the final mark to us.
There is one resubmission opportunity per NEA assignment.

All work submitted (or resubmitted) must be based on the assignment that is live for
the series of submission.

For information about feedback see section 6. The final piece of work must be
completed solely by the student and teachers must not detail specifically what
amendments should be made.

