•	 are appropriate and in line with ethical standards
and your centre’s safeguarding responsibilities.

Suitable to the needs of the student

We are committed to ensuring that achievement of
these qualifications is free from unnecessary barriers.

Observation and questioning

The primary evidence for assessment is the work
submitted by the student, however we consider the
following assessment methods suitable for teachers/
assessors to use for these qualifications:

•	 observation of a student doing something

•	 questioning of the student or witness.

Observation

You and the student should plan observations together,
but it is your responsibility to record the observation
properly (for example observing a student undertaking
a practical task). Find more information in the Teacher
Observation Records section below.

