6.4.3

Internal standardisation

It is important that all teachers/assessors work to
common standards. Centres must make sure that,
within each unit, the internal standardisation of marks
across teachers/assessors and teaching groups takes
place using an appropriate procedure.

This can be done in a number of ways. In the first year,
reference material and OCR training meetings will
provide a basis for centres’ own standardisation. In
following years, this, or centres’ own archive material,
may be used. We advise centres to hold preliminary
meetings of staff involved to compare standards
through cross-marking a small sample of work. After
most marking has been completed, a further meeting
at which work is exchanged and discussed will help
final adjustments to be made.

