marks for that task.

Teachers/assessors should use the full range of marks
available to them and award full marks in any band for
work that fully meets that descriptor. This is work that
is ‘the best one could expect from students working at
that level’.

If you have given additional, more specific support or
guidance to an individual student to get them started
on a task, because they could not start a task or part of
a task that was critical to them accessing the rest of
the task or assignment, this must be recorded on the
student’s work and/or Unit Recording Sheet (URS) for
our Moderator to see (see Section 6.3). In this situation,
the student should not be awarded the marks for
the work for which they received help, and the marks
achieved must be adjusted appropriately. Recording
this on the student’s work and/or URS will help our
Moderator to understand why the marks have not been
awarded.

If you’re the only assessor in your centre for this
