  "type": "8 marks — Discuss / Evaluate (Extended Response)",
  "marks": "Mastering (7-8 marks): Response discusses safety procedures, safety measures AND security measures with clear distinction between the first two. Applies at least three examples from the spec content to the named setting (GP surgery) with reference to the specific service user groups (elderly, children, mental health). Builds chains of reasoning linking each procedure or measure to a specific protection outcome. Reaches an evaluative judgement, for example evaluating whether procedures (which require training and commitment from all staff) are harder to maintain than measures (which are physical and automatic), or considering the balance between security and service users' rights (e.g. locked doors may feel restrictive but protect vulnerable patients). Uses precise terminology throughout.\n\nSecure (5-6 marks): Covers most categories with mostly accurate application to the named setting. Uses some precise terminology. Points are mostly developed. May lack a fully supported evaluative judgement or one well-developed chain of reasoning.\n\nDeveloping (3-4 marks): Relevant content but limited development. May conflate procedures and measures. Limited application to the named setting. Points stated rather than analysed.\n\nEmerging (1-2 marks): Basic points about safety or security with little or no application to the GP surgery or the specific service user groups. Listing rather than discussing or evaluating."
